From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Moussalem <george.moussalem@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 17:27:49 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: winbond: add support for W25N01KW chips

Add support for the Winbond W25N01KW, a 1.8 V 1 Gbit SPI-NAND. It is
second-sourced on the Xiaomi AX3000T v2 in place of the ESMT F50D1G41LB,
and without an ID table entry the probe fails on those units:

  spi-nand spi0.0: unknown raw ID efbe210000

Per the datasheet (W25N01KWxxxG/T/R, rev. D) and the chip's parameter
page, the part has 2048 byte pages with 64 bytes of spare, 64 pages per
block, 1024 blocks and at most 20 bad blocks, and needs 4-bit ECC per
512 bytes. The on-die ECC keeps its parity in a separate 32-byte area
outside the spare. It reports the maximum bit flip count in bits 6:4 of
feature register 0x30, which is what w25n02kv_ecc_get_status() reads, so
use it as for the W25N01KV.

The K-generation OOB layouts place the ECC bytes past offset 64, so use
the w25m02gv layout of the W25N01GV/GW, which have the same 64-byte
spare. It marks bytes the chip leaves to the user as ECC, which only
under-reports the free OOB bytes. On qualcommax the QPIC is the ECC
engine and the chip's layout is not used at all.

Signed-off-by: George Moussalem <george.moussalem@outlook.com>
[use the w25m02gv OOB layout, the w25n02kv one does not fit in 64 bytes;
 describe the part from its datasheet]
Reported-by: Mikhail Zhilkin <csharper2005@gmail.com>
Link: https://forum.openwrt.org/t/adding-support-for-xiaomi-ax3000t-rd03v2/235136/17
Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/winbond.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/winbond.c
@@ -457,6 +457,15 @@ static const struct spinand_info winbond
 					      &update_cache_variants),
 		     0,
 		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&w25n01kv_ooblayout, w25n02kv_ecc_get_status)),
+	SPINAND_INFO("W25N01KW",
+		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0xbe, 0x21),
+		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 1024, 20, 1, 1, 1),
+		     NAND_ECCREQ(4, 512),
+		     SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
+					      &write_cache_variants,
+					      &update_cache_variants),
+		     0,
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&w25m02gv_ooblayout, w25n02kv_ecc_get_status)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("W35N01JW", /* 1.8V */
 		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0xdc, 0x21),
 		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 4096, 128, 64, 512, 10, 1, 1, 1),
